From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1185 redfin: AMP: SweetCLPC under both schedulers (sched_amp PLACE
 via sched_perfcontrol_thread_group_recommend, launch boost)

1182's SweetCLPC moves from osfmk/kern/sched_clutch.c (compiled out with sched_amp) to the new
osfmk/kern/sweet_clpc.c (osfmk/conf/files: standard; body under SWEET_AMP && CONFIG_THREAD_GROUPS).
Edge behaviour is unchanged: sched_clutch.c keeps sweet_edge_policy and calls sweet_clpc_policy_adjust()
(now with the P cluster id as an argument) and sweet_clpc_tick(); it exports sweet_edge_clpc_pcluster()
and sweet_edge_clpc_reapply() (walk under sweet_edge_mtx). SweetCLPC has its own sweet_clpc_mtx
(lock order sweet_clpc_mtx -> sweet_edge_mtx -> tg_lock).
sched_amp (SWEET_AMP_SCHED_AMP 1):
 - PLACE = the native CLPC call sched_perfcontrol_thread_group_recommend() per user group:
   UI groups P; others E with kern.sweet_clpc_amp_other 1 (default) or SMP with 0; PLACE off -> SMP.
   Walk in the SweetCLPC thread call on UI_APP changes, new UI work intervals, new groups, mask changes.
 - kern.sweet_clpc_amp_rt 1 (default): RT / fixed threads of user tasks in E-recommended groups stay
   P-eligible (recommended_pset_type(), processor.c; flag sweet_clpc_amp_rt_p).
 - FREQ's P waiting load: P load average above the recommended P core count.
 - sweet_amp_tick (5 s, sched_amp.c) calls sweet_clpc_tick(); the SWEET CLPC 5 s line prints whenever
   the mask is non-zero and ends "| rec P a E b SMP c (tgs P x E y SMP z) | launch n".
Both: kern.sweet_clpc_launch_ms (default 0 = off; needs FREQ): UI_APP set -> gold/prime need at the top
step for N ms (0964 caps remain the ceiling), governor kicked from the thread call.
kern.sweet_clpc* sysctls move out of the CONFIG_SCHED_EDGE block (both schedulers); amp_other/amp_rt read -1
and refuse writes on Edge.

---
